       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 50 mg is well above the usual range for amlodipine. The maximum recommended adult dose is 10 mg once daily, and 50 mg is five times that. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects could last for days. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change this.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n\nIf you do want 50 mg, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
